id: 6
hanzi: 所谓
pinyin: suǒ wèi
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Adjective

meanings_summary:
  en: so-called; what is called; what is known as
  es: el llamado; lo que se conoce como; el presunto

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Adjective | Standard | what is meant by or commonly called; explaining terminology | lo que comúnmente se denomina o entiende por tal concepto | 所谓四合，即四面房屋围在一起 (the so-called 'four-join' means houses on four sides)
  2 | Adjective | Standard | so-called (used skeptically or disapprovingly to denote false claims) | presunto o supuesto con matiz escéptico o irónico | 别相信那些所谓专家的养生秘诀 (don't trust those so-called experts' secrets)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 所谓四合院，‘四’指东、西、南、北四面，‘合’则是四面房屋围在一起，形成封闭的方形院落。 | Suǒwèi sìhéyuàn, 'sì' zhǐ dōng, xī, nán, běi sì miàn, 'hé' zé shì sì miàn fángwū wéi zài yìqǐ, xíngchéng fēngbì de fāngxíng yuànluò. | As for the so-called siheyuan, 'four' signifies the four directions, while 'join' means enclosing houses on four sides into a private square courtyard. | En el llamado siheyuan, 'cuatro' alude a los cuatro puntos cardinales y 'juntar' describe cuatro pabellones abrazando un patio cuadrado íntimo.
  #2 | 消费者应当保持理性清醒，切勿轻信网络上那些未经权威科学认证的所谓‘抗衰老神药’。 | Xiāofèizhě yīngdāng bǎochí lǐxìng qīngxǐng, qièwù qīngxìn wǎngluò shang nàxiē wèijīng quánwēi kēxué rènzhèng de suǒwèi 'kàng shuāilǎo shényào'. | Consumers should stay rational and avoid falling for uncertified 'anti-aging miracles' touted by so-called medical gurus online. | Los consumidores deben mantener la cautela y desconfiar de los supuestos 'remedios milagrosos antiedad' que proliferan en internet sin aval científico.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  所谓四合 | the so-called four-join
  所谓专家 | so-called experts
  所谓的成功 | so-called success
  无所谓 | doesn't matter; indifferent
  所谓何事 | what is this concerning (formal)
  所谓事实 | the alleged facts

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  顾名思义 | gù míng sī yì | as the name implies; self-explanatory from the name
  名不副实 | míng bù fù shí | the name does not match the reality; unworthy of the name
  开宗明义 | kāi zōng míng yì | state the primary purpose right at the beginning
  理所当然 | lǐ suǒ dāng rán | taken for granted; natural and proper as a matter of course

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  所 | suǒ | place; particle indicating receiver of action | lugar; partícula que sustantiva el objeto | 斤 | axe | 户 (single door) + 斤 (axe chopping timber on doorstep) | 所 (suǒ) | 8 | 左右结构 | An axe 斤 chopping wood at a homestead door 户; originally the designated chopping spot, developing into places and passive pronoun particle. | Setting down an axe (斤) at the wooden threshold (户) to mark an established dwelling place (所). | Apoyar el hacha (斤) en el umbral de la puerta (户) para señalar el lugar de asiento (所). | 214 | HSHML | 所
  谓 | wèi | say; speak of; call; meaning | decir; llamar; denominar; significar | 讠 | speech | 讠 (spoken words) + 胃 (stomach / inner intent) | 胃 (wèi / phonetic) | 11 | 左右结构 | Speech radical 讠 beside stomach 胃; voicing words that express what is harbored in one's stomach/mind. | Uttering spoken words (讠) straight from the gut (胃) to name and define a truth (谓). | Pronunciar palabras claras (讠) que brotan de las entrañas (胃) para nombrar las cosas (谓). | 51 | IWBG | 謂

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: What (所) is stated and named by spoken words (谓) defines the so-called term (所谓).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Aquello (所) que se enuncia y denomina con palabras (谓) es lo que se llama (所谓).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Essential classical expository marker (所谓的 'what is termed...') used in academic definition and dialectical skepticism.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dipping third tone followed by falling fourth tone: 'suǒ wèi' (214-51). Dip low on 'suǒ', then descend decisively on 'wèi'.

