semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 所谓 introduces an explicit definition of a concept or expresses ironic skepticism toward a label.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 所谓 vs. 名义 | míngyì | 名义 is a noun meaning titular capacity or pretext (以朋友的名义), while 所谓 is a modifier explaining definitions or questioning authenticity.
    2 | 所谓 vs. 据说 | jùshuō | 据说 introduces reported hearsay from outside sources (据说要下雨), while 所谓 defines terminology or questions validity.
    3 | 所谓 vs. 称作 | chēngzuò | 称作 is a transitive predicate verb meaning 'to be called' (这种鸟被称作翠鸟), while 所谓 is an attributive modifier.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 探寻传统建筑之美，必须先理解其造字立意的文化源头。所谓四合，‘四’指东、西、南、北四面房屋，‘合’则是四面房屋围合在一起。这简简单单的两个汉字，生动凝练地勾勒出了北方民居中正平和的审美意境。 | Tànxún chuántǒng jiànzhù zhī měi, bìxū xiān lǐjiě qí zàozì lìyì de wénhuà yuántóu. Suǒwèi sìhé, 'sì' zhǐ dōng, xī, nán, běi sì miàn fángwū, 'hé' zé shì sì miàn fángwū wéihé zài yìqǐ. Zhè jiǎnjiǎn-dāndān de liǎng ge Hànzì, shēngdòng níngliàn de gōulè chū le běifāng mínjū zhōngzhèng-pínghé de shěnměi yìjìng. | Exploring the beauty of architecture requires understanding cultural etymology. The 'four-join' implies buildings on four sides enclosing a yard. These two characters sketch the harmonious aesthetic core of northern vernacular homes. | Para apreciar la arquitectura tradicional conviene desentrañar sus raíces léxicas. Lo de 'cuatro juntas' define pabellones en los cuatro rumbos cerrándose en torno al patio, compendiando la serena armonía solariega.
  #2 | 在快节奏的商业炒作中，不少打着所谓‘传统古建’旗号的新建仿古街区，由于过度追求商业利益而丧失了原汁原味的民俗烟火气。真正值得我们倍加珍视的，从来不是冰冷的水泥仿品，而是老北京四合院里世代相传的质朴温情。 | Zài kuài jiézòu de shāngyè chǎozuò zhōng, bùshǎo dǎ zhe suǒwèi 'chuántǒng gǔjiàn' qíhào de xīnjiàn fǎnggǔ jiēqū, yóuyú guòdù zhuīqiú shāngyè lìyì ér sàngshī le yuánzhī-yuánwèi de mínsú yānhuǒqì. Zhēnzhèng zhíde wǒmen bèijiā zhēnshì de, cónglái búshì bīnglěng de shuǐní fǎngpǐn, érshì lǎo Běijīng sìhéyuàn lǐ shìdài-xiāngchuán de zhípǔ wēnqíng. | Amid commercial hype, many new pedestrian streets under so-called 'heritage' banners forfeit authentic community life in greed. What deserves cherishing is never cold concrete facsimiles, but the timeless warmth preserved in old courtyards. | Entre el bullicio mercantil, muchos recintos que se anuncian como 'patrimonio histórico' pierden su autenticidad por el lucro. Lo que de veras vale la pena rescatar es el calor humano vivo de los patios tradicionales.
